From: P16 N1X Linux integration <n1x@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/libplacebo: allow Vulkan queues with libplacebo API 360

libplacebo versions before API 365 have no queue flags field in
pl_vulkan_queue. FFmpeg 9.0.2 rejects every nonzero Vulkan queue flag even
though it can still pass the queue family index and count to libplacebo.
The N1X Vulkan device reports VK_QUEUE_TRANSFER_BIT, so that check aborts
filter initialization before a frame is processed. Omit only the unavailable
field on older libplacebo APIs. The API 365+ path remains unchanged.

---
 libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c b/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
--- a/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
@@ -659,8 +659,7 @@
 #if PL_API_VER >= 365
     pl_qf->flags = hwctx->queue_flags;
 #else
-    if (hwctx->queue_flags != 0)
-        return AVERROR(EINVAL); // prevent undefined behavior
+    /* Older libplacebo accepts only the queue family index and count. */
 #endif
     return 0;
 }
